1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,289
Every design meeting needs a diagram.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,423
So we spend twenty minutes drawing boxes and
arrows…

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,068
and we're left with five minutes to explain
them.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,173
That's why we built Draft Canvas: to flip
that.

5
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:17,610
Now your coding agent can sit right beside
you, on the canvas.

6
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:20,651
Meet Nodi!

7
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:25,127
Ask what could go wrong, and it answers on
your diagram.

8
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:29,697
Ask for a change. You decide.

9
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:34,302
Compare before and after. Nothing changes
until you accept it.

10
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:39,750
And now, the part that matters most:
explaining it.

11
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:45,537
Start with the whole system, then step into
a service, down to its components.

12
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:48,353
Then present the flow, step by step.

13
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,312
Your architecture stays on your device.

14
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:54,897
Your agent is the one you already use.

15
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,871
And every decision is yours.

16
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,572
Free and open source.

17
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:05,156
So, the next design meeting: five minutes of
boxes and arrows — and twenty of explaining!

18
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:06,977
Draw less. Explain more.
